```
With flex-wrap, each group can wrap internally? `dock-group` is a flex container; if it doesn't shrink, groups stay together. The weapon group (2), mat group (3), piece group (3) = 3 units; total widths ~2*46=92, 3*46=138, 3*46=138 → 368 + gaps 8 + padding 8 = 384 > 374. Flex-wrap on action-dock will wrap the last group to next row, yielding 2 rows: row1 weapons+mats (230), row2 pieces (138). That looks uneven but acceptable. Better to make each group flex-wrap? Or set dock-group flex:1 and buttons flexible.

Alternative: at max-width 560, use a grid with 8 columns? Each 38px = 304 + gaps 28 = 332, fits. Use `.action-dock { display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(8, minmax(0,1fr)); }` and `.dock-group { display: contents; }` so all 8 buttons become grid items; dividers hidden. Then buttons ~ (374-28)/8=43px. Labels 7px fit. This is clean! But `.dock-group { display: contents; }` removes group gaps; add column-gap 4. Buttons fill equal width. Row 1 only. Great.

